      "title": "Setup and model downloads",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FastH3 compact VSA performance\n\nThis graph uses the native ~35.05B FastH3 VSA student, not the LTX-2.5 22B model. The 4.0-second request aligns to H3's required 107 frames (4.458 seconds at 24 fps).\n\n1. Install WeeTodd Nodes and restart ComfyUI.\n2. Download the H3 components and converted FastH3 transformer listed below.\n3. Keep the relative Component Loader paths unchanged.\n4. Queue the workflow after reviewing **FastH3 Profile and Hardware Advisories** and after **H3 Preflight** succeeds.\n\n### H3 downloads\n\n- [Official MiniMax H3 partition, processor, tokenizer, and audio VAE](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3)\n  Save the repository under `ComfyUI/models/MiniMax-H3`.\n- [Official FastH3 VSA student](https://huggingface.co/FastVideo/FastVideo-FastH3-4-step-Preview-v1-VSA-DataFree)\n  Convert it with `scripts/convert_fastvideo_fasth3.py` and save the result under `ComfyUI/models/MiniMax-H3/transformers/weetodd-fasth3-vsa-datafree-q8-paged`.\n- [Qwen3-VL Q8 paged conditioner](https://huggingface.co/Vayden/Qwen3-VL-32B-H3-MLX-q8-paged)\n  Save it under `ComfyUI/models/MiniMax-H3/text_encoders/q8-paged`.\n- [MiniMax H3 video VAE MLX Q8](https://huggingface.co/Vayden/MiniMax-H3-Video-VAE-MLX-Q8)\n  Save it under `ComfyUI/models/MiniMax-H3/vae/q8`.\n\nThe recommended profile uses compact indexed Metal VSA. Select the Conservative profile in the FastH3 Production Profile node for the grouped MLX fallback. Fused QKV is explicitly experimental. Leave the advanced advisory memory budget at 0 to use detected memory; manual values test warnings only and do not simulate smaller hardware."
      ],
      "color": "#243447",
      "bgcolor": "#15202b"
    },
